Z||000000||GTMike||08-01-2001||01:07 AM||||oh shoot lol  i ment a shift light.   i can't changed the subject  with the edit option<P>i'll get to my point.   i need a shift light. a nice bright light to tell me when its at 5k.  i keep hitting the rev limiter in first gear.    i'm keeping my eyes on the road instead of my tack.  is there any way to wire up a shift light to the stock rpm gage??<P>thanks<p>[This message has been edited by GTMike (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-01-2001||03:19 AM||||Do you run the other gears that high?<BR>Train your ear to the tune of 3500 RPM's as your shift point. Doesn't your shift light work on the cluster?||||reg||1
Z||000002||862M4inCA||08-01-2001||09:06 AM||||From my personal experience my shift light works at any RPM above 2K. Anytime I sustain an engine speed or am gradually accelerating above 2K and the computer determines I could "save gas" by shifting to a higher gear it iluminates the shift light. Hhowever if I really jump on it the light doesn't come on until I'm a couple hundred RPM's into the red zone.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||08-01-2001||11:23 AM||||You can hook it to the white tach wire in the harness behing the tach area of the inst. pod. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||08-01-2001||12:54 PM||||The Fiero shift light is a "smart" one.  I wish I could have retained it(no more stock computer).  Does anyone have the electronic ability to make a curcuit that duplicates the stock light?<P>The thing apparently figures out how fast you are accelerating(from the VSS) vs. RPMs and if you are "losing" acceleration it tells you to shift.<P>This would be cool...I'd wire some super bright LEDs to it.  If anyone can do it or knows of one available let me know!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||GTMike||08-01-2001||01:47 PM||||umm i didn't know my car had a shift light  it must not work.   anyways this is for raceing  lol.  not just everyday driveing.   i can handle that.  lol.  you must have though i was retarted.   <P><BR>where the heck wouuld the stock one be located????   any way to change what rpm it tells you to shift at.  i need one at 5000 so i'm shifting before the rev limiter kicks on. <P>i only really need it in first gear. cause it revs soo fast.  with my new intake and no cat.   and soon to be under drive pully it will rev even faster. <P>thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Joe Torma||08-01-2001||02:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTMike:<BR><B>umm i didn't know my car had a shift light  it must not work. <P><BR>where the heck wouuld the stock one be located????   any way to change what rpm it tells you to shift at.  i need one at 5000 so i'm shifting before the rev limiter kicks on. <P>i only really need it in first gear. cause it revs soo fast.  with my new intake and no cat.   and soon to be under drive pully it will rev even faster. <P>thanks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think 1st gear is for pulling tree stumps.  The light is on the top right.  your bulb must be out.  Easy to fix. <P>Hmmm...idea...you could always stick a flashlight on your dash and wire it into the stock shift light!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Uh, or just get one from Summit with the interchangeable RPM chips.<P>Joe<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||84Bill||08-01-2001||02:42 PM||||Do what Indiana said. I would sit in my car and rev the engine to 1000 rpm and close my eyes then hit the gas a few times then try to find the same sound and take a peek at the tach to see how close I was. Id do this at intervals of 500 rpm up to 3500 until I knew exactly what rpm the engne was turning just by the sound the engine made. <BR>After that I'd drive the car and "guess" the rpm and speed then "Verify" by glancing quickly at the tach and speedo.<BR>I can accuratly tell how fast I'm going by the sound of the engine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Old timers call this (among other things) driving by the seat of your pants.||||reg||14
Z||000008||Posthumane||08-01-2001||03:03 PM||||Easy to do when your on city streets, but at the start of a race you can't hear your own engine a lot of the times. What I think would be cool is if you got an after market heads-up display tach. That way you can see the tach and watch the road at the same time.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Pontiaddict||08-01-2001||03:36 PM||||The facrory shift light also takes coolant temp and throttle angle into account and it tells you to shift earlier when the car is cold and depending on how far your foot is down on the throttle.||||reg||1
